Subject: [PATCH 6/7] Preserve typed image precision in solid fills and cache
 accounting

Read one-pixel images into explicit nonlinear-sRGB float RGBA with separate alpha and preserve extended colour through the optimized Skia fill. Count actual raster row storage or a typed nominal GPU estimate, refuse checked cache-size overflow, and retain each selected source cost before clearing its image. Prepare one-pixel drawing and padded-row clear regressions.

No compiler or tests were run; native object, internal ABI/vtable link and behavioral qualification remain pending.
